###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy and force RMSEs are shown only in Figs. 1-3; the text gives approximate values ('at most a few meV/atom and around 0.06 eV/A' for crystals, 'around 10 meV/atom and 0.3 eV/A' for liquids), which are not encoded.
# - Speed is given only relative to other potentials (tabGAP 175 times faster than the untabulated GAP-3b+EAM; GAP-SOAP about 65 times slower than tabGAP), not as timings.
# - Bulk, surface, defect, thermal and liquid properties (Tables II-III) are property comparisons with 15 literature EAM/MEAM/ABOP/ADP potentials and GAP-D18, which are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/byggmastar2022multiscale.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
